# Shared rules vendored via osac-ai-skills (OSAC-4006): symlinks materialized
# by tools/link-agent-skills.sh, not committed. Workspace-only rules (e.g.
# cross-repo-workflow.md) stay real files and remain tracked. (.claude/agents/
# needs no entry here — no !.claude/agents/ exception above, so the blanket
# .claude/* ignore already covers vendored agent symlinks like quick-fix.md.)
.claude/rules/architecture-patterns.md
.claude/rules/networking-design-alignment.md
.claude/rules/request-path-tracing.md
.claude/rules/dev-conventions.md

# Shared hook documentation vendored via osac-ai-skills (OSAC-4006): symlink
# materialized by tools/link-agent-skills.sh, not committed. The actual hook
# scripts (update-ai-context.sh, statusline.sh) are workspace-specific
# executables and stay real, tracked files — only the generic README.md moved.
.claude/hooks/README.md

